// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - KurstFiles 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2817340041" "Agent Kurst's files"
// DetailString :
"P52003543" "These files, composed by Longbow Agent Kurst, detail the many ciphers he has successfully broken while working on Mercy Island. Although many of these ciphers originated with Arachnos, some of them are the codes Burke uses to correspond with his clients."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3602355930" "You know my code of honor, {VillainName}? None. I'll steal from anyone if the price is right. From Arachnos, from Longbow, even from the Snakes if they had anything worth taking.  <A HREF={ACCEPT}>But on this particular day, we're going after the good guys.</A> Longbow. Saviors of Paragon City, thorn in the side of Arachnos. Truth is, I don't mind Longbow so much. They irritate Arachnos, which I can't help but find entertaining. Trouble is, Longbow's got something I want."
// AcceptString :
"P2061964287" "Go after the good guys"
// SendOffString :
"P1886719362" "Longbow's got some of the best cryptographers this side of Paragon City. One of them is known as Agent Kurst. I need Kurst's files. Not only do they contain a wealth of knowledge about Arachnos ciphers, they also are likely to contain a mention or two about the codes my clients use. Which means, I'm sorry to say, Kurst isn't long for this world."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2246089383" "Defeat Kurst and his guards"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3121742327" "I need Kurst's files, {VillainName}. And now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1719937904" "Longbow must have some serious funding."

